  "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Lanterns Underroot reusable terrain TERRAIN TILE atlas for a hand-painted 2D side-scroller. ONE SQUARE image tightly divided into EXACTLY FOUR EQUAL COLUMNS and FOUR EQUAL ROWS, 16 equal square cells, no gutters or margins, full canvas used. Exactly four tiles per row, never three rows of three plus a strip. Each root platform module is interwoven broad brown tree roots forming platform segments, restrained bark ridges, no grass moss rocks or glow, no branches, fruit, lanterns, blossoms, plants, ruins, glows, shadows, arches or scenery. Front orthographic elevation, no perspective. Exact content reading order: row1: root platform left end; root platform repeat middle; root platform right end; isolated single solid terrain block. Row2: vertical left terrain wall; opaque full square interior specified material fill NO holes; vertical right wall; repeatable narrow ledge middle. Row3: outer bottom-left terrain corner; repeatable terrain underside; outer bottom-right terrain corner; narrow ledge left cap. Row4: narrow ledge right cap; 45-degree rising slope; 45-degree falling slope; three-step ascending terrain stairs. Solid fill reaches all connecting cell edges, never floating decorative islands inside tiles. Use only specified material; no added decorative plants. All modules fit own cell, connecting edges match, empty outside corners are genuinely alpha-zero transparent. No text, numbers, labels or drawn grid. Designed for 64px export per tile. Crisp readable game tiles, restrained painterly texture and muted green/brown/blue-gray palette. Background transparent.",
